    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 60 tests pass \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**, no failures or errors.\n\n## Summary\n\nI moved the date-derived values onto a fiscal-year basis (fiscal year starting 1 July, named by the calendar year it ends in \u2014 the Australian convention this app already implies via NSW/VIC/QLD localities and Australian public holidays).\n\n**New utility \u2014 `util/FiscalYears.java`:**\n- `fiscalYear(date)` \u2192 numeric fiscal year (a date on/after 1 July belongs to the next calendar year's FY).\n- `fiscalYearLabel(date)` \u2192 `'FY<YY>'` (e.g. `FY27` for Aug 2026), null-safe.\n- `elapsedFiscalYears(from, to)` \u2192 count of 1-July boundaries crossed.\n\n**`util/Memberships.java`:** tenure now counts elapsed fiscal years instead of 365-day windows. Replaced `TENURE_LEVEL_DAYS = 365` with `TENURE_LEVEL_FISCAL_YEARS = 1`; `hasQualifyingTenure` now uses `FiscalYears.elapsedFiscalYears(regDate, now) > 1`. A brand-new owner still has zero elapsed fiscal years, so the existing points/level tests (Cp39, Cp40) stay green.\n\n**`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`:**\n- Added `fiscalYear` mapping \u2192 `FiscalYears.fiscalYearLabel(registrationDate)`.\n- Changed `membershipNumber`'s year segment from calendar year to the fiscal year's last two digits, so it stays consistent with `fiscalYear` (verified by Cp14).\n\n**`resources/openapi.yml`:** added the read-only `fiscalYear` property (so the DTO is generated) and updated the `membershipNumber` / `membershipPoints` descriptions to reflect the fiscal-year basis.\n\nSince the stored `registrationDate` is already business-day-adjusted in `addOwner` (`toBusinessDay`), all fiscal-year derivations naturally operate on the adjusted date. Observed at runtime: a today-registered owner rolls to `2026-08-17` and gets `FY27` / `...-M27`.",
